 "\\frac{3}{2}\\displaystyle \\int_{π/2}^{11π/6}\\sin^{2} (2θ + \\frac{π}{3})dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155914} {:answer/id #uuid "a8442735-77c4-52be-b4fe-93d11de21881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\displaystyle \\int_{π/3}^{4π/3}\\sin^{2} (2θ + \\frac{π}{3})dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155915} {:answer/id #uuid "b33793d1-ef84-589d-a273-3640a97994d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{- π/6}^{4π/3}\\sin^{2} (2θ + \\frac{π}{3})dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155916} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c5adc8-9255-50c9-b733-4ac24638cba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{- π/6}^{11π/6}\\sin^{2} (2θ + \\frac{π}{3})dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155917} {:answer/id #uuid "1b2547f9-597f-5408-b4c8-44bc979009ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{- π/6}^{5π/6}\\sin^{2} (2θ + \\frac{π}{3})dθ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155918}] :answer-field/id #uuid "676f7b35-5434-55eb-ad55-37dab460907b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155913}] :question/id #uuid "c7ae6625-2462-5c24-ab37-c40b68057a97" :question/math-academy-id "q-83527" :question/problem "![](images/3a/3aa82e021a1871bd17abfd72570452bc6aefe358a8fddd3cb8e92bb6ff91c5a9.png)\n\nThe area of one loop of the polar curve $r = \\sqrt{2}\\sin (2θ + \\frac{π}{3})$ (shown above) is given by the integral\n$A = \\displaystyle \\int_{- π/6}^{π/3}\\sin^{2} (2θ + \\frac{π}{3})dθ$.\nWhich of the following represents the total area bounded by the polar curve?"}]}
